From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:54:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 309/311] avcodec/mpeg12dec: hand D-pictures only to hwaccels
 that decode them

The MPEG-1 hwaccel change passed every picture with picture_coding_type 4
to any active hwaccel as an I-picture. That also covered MPEG-2 streams,
where the value is invalid, and the VDPAU, NVDEC and VideoToolbox MPEG-1
hwaccels, which cannot decode D-pictures and would now decode their DC-only
slices as I-picture slices instead of the picture being rejected.

Add HWACCEL_CAP_MPEG1_D_PICTURES, set it on the V4L2 Request MPEG-1/2
hwaccels (the only ones that pass V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_D on) and take
the D-picture path only for MPEG-1 streams with such a hwaccel. Everything
else rejects D-pictures as before.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 libavcodec/hwaccel_internal.h   | 7 +++++++
 libavcodec/mpeg12dec.c          | 6 ++++--
 libavcodec/v4l2_request_mpeg2.c | 3 ++-
 3 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/hwaccel_internal.h b/libavcodec/hwaccel_internal.h
index 2d03f39c77..9daf7051eb 100644
--- a/libavcodec/hwaccel_internal.h
+++ b/libavcodec/hwaccel_internal.h
@@ -37,6 +37,13 @@
  * parsed into the decoder context (mb_x, mb_y, qscale).
  */
 #define HWACCEL_CAP_RESYNC_SLICES   (1 << 2)
+/**
+ * The hwaccel decodes MPEG-1 D-pictures (picture_coding_type 4, DC
+ * coefficients only). The MPEG-1/2 decoder hands such pictures to it as
+ * I-pictures with MPVContext.mpeg1_d_picture set; without this capability
+ * they are rejected as before.
+ */
+#define HWACCEL_CAP_MPEG1_D_PICTURES (1 << 3)
 
 typedef struct FFHWAccel {
     /**
diff --git a/libavcodec/mpeg12dec.c b/libavcodec/mpeg12dec.c
index 1a52f87b77..9ec54af2ad 100644
--- a/libavcodec/mpeg12dec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/mpeg12dec.c
@@ -995,8 +995,10 @@ static int mpeg1_decode_picture(AVCodecContext *avctx, const uint8_t *buf,
     ref = get_bits(gb, 10); /* temporal ref */
     s->pict_type = get_bits(gb, 3);
     s->mpeg1_d_picture = 0;
-    /* D-pictures: only a hwaccel can decode them; carry them as I-pictures. */
-    if (s->pict_type == 4 && avctx->hwaccel) {
+    /* D-pictures: only some hwaccels decode them; carry them as I-pictures. */
+    if (s->pict_type == 4 && avctx->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_MPEG1VIDEO &&
+        avctx->hwaccel &&
+        (ffhwaccel(avctx->hwaccel)->caps_internal & HWACCEL_CAP_MPEG1_D_PICTURES)) {
         s->mpeg1_d_picture = 1;
         s->pict_type       = AV_PICTURE_TYPE_I;
     }
diff --git a/libavcodec/v4l2_request_mpeg2.c b/libavcodec/v4l2_request_mpeg2.c
index 28b625e416..e8493f00d4 100644
--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_request_mpeg2.c
+++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_request_mpeg2.c
@@ -204,7 +204,8 @@ const FFHWAccel ff_ ## codec ## _v4l2request_hwaccel = {                     \
     .uninit             = ff_v4l2_request_uninit,                            \
     .priv_data_size     = sizeof(V4L2RequestContext),                        \
     .frame_params       = v4l2_request_mpeg2_frame_params,                   \
-    .caps_internal      = HWACCEL_CAP_ASYNC_SAFE,                            \
+    .caps_internal      = HWACCEL_CAP_ASYNC_SAFE |                           \
+                          HWACCEL_CAP_MPEG1_D_PICTURES,                      \
 };
 
 #if CONFIG_MPEG1_V4L2REQUEST_HWACCEL
